description:
Develop a 4-to-2 priority encoder. This module takes a 4-bit input and outputs a 2-bit representation of the highest priority active input signal. If multiple inputs are active, the encoder prioritizes the highest-order bit (e.g., if both 'in[3]' and 'in[2]' are high, it will output the code corresponding to 'in[3]'). The output defaults to '11' when no input is asserted.
module top_module(
    input [3:0] in,
    output reg [1:0] out
);

code:
module top_module(
    input [3:0] in,
    output reg [1:0] out
);always @ (in) begin
    case (in)
        4'b0001: out = 2'b00;
        4'b0010: out = 2'b01;
        4'b0100: out = 2'b10;
        4'b1000: out = 2'b11;
        default: out = 2'b11;
    endcase
end

endmodule

